WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 28 Leader Video
Unit 7, Lesson 4: Hell

1
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.354
Several years ago,

2
00:00:07.354 --> 00:00:13.250
I was teaching one of my Bible classes and a really important and significant book

3
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.060
in the lives of most evangelical Christians came out.

4
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:22.388
And it created a firestorm of conversation, waves of controversy,

5
00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:27.060
and all kinds of things happening in the Christian world.

6
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.089
The book was Love Wins by Rob Bell,

7
00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:33.785
and I had all kinds of parents asking me if we were going to read it or demanding

8
00:00:33.785 --> 00:00:35.060
that we don't read it.

9
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:40.840
I had students asking me about it, so I finally said enough is enough,

10
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.060
I need to figure out what the story is.

11
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:49.060
So I read it, and I used it as a discussion point for my students.

12
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.560
Now, the book had an incredible way of bringing up some really,

13
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.060
really important topics to discuss.

14
00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:01.932
But what was interesting was that the students seemed to really gravitate toward

15
00:01:01.932 --> 00:01:04.060
what the book was suggesting.

16
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:09.069
That we somehow have this endless sort of chance by chance,

17
00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:13.060
or chance after chance cycle of getting to God.

18
00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.060
That if we don't, if we miss it the first time, we'll get a second try at it.

19
00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:22.060
And that the idea of hell is really not all that accurate.

20
00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:22.248
Now,

21
00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:26.060
it's an interesting conversation piece and something that we ought to talk about.

22
00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.060
But the Bible is pretty clear.

23
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.925
Now, we've talked about the reliability of this text,

24
00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:36.060
and Jesus is really clear that hell exists.

25
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:40.675
But it's so easy for our students to want to discount that because we don't

26
00:01:40.675 --> 00:01:44.060
necessarily want to be held accountable to our actions.

27
00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:48.060
And we don't really want to face the consequences. Who wants to face consequences?

28
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.060
So the questions often asked me, like, okay, well, what is hell like?

29
00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.318
I don't know. It's probably not nice. I don't really know.

30
00:01:55.318 --> 00:01:57.060
I don't know if I want to know.

31
00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.060
It's not God.

32
00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:05.060
Hell is the tragic consequence of rejecting God.

33
00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:12.060
So to help your students understand what this tragic consequence would be like,

34
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:17.999
the intro experience takes them through sort of a mini journey of imagining the best

35
00:02:17.999 --> 00:02:19.060
possible place,

36
00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:25.060
the favorite place, why you love it, describe it, even put pictures in there.

37
00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:32.380
And then remove all of its goodness, everything.

38
00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:35.380
Cross out any word that has good meaning.

39
00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:40.698
Remove all benefits from that place, all value, all joy, refreshing qualities,

40
00:02:40.698 --> 00:02:41.380
all of it.

41
00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.380
What would that place be like then?

42
00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:50.380
And that should help them get into that space of what hell would be like.

43
00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:54.380
I often describe it to students of think of it this way.

44
00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:59.380
Common grace is the grace that God provides all of us, right?

45
00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:03.090
The fact that God is sustaining this world, every breath that I take,

46
00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.380
the sun that is shining,

47
00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:09.380
the air that is blowing, the trees growing, all the rain that falls,

48
00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:15.973
all of the things that happen on the righteous and the unrighteous are all common

49
00:03:15.973 --> 00:03:16.380
grace

50
00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:21.380
because God is here, active in moving in history

51
00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:27.380
and participating in sort of sovereignly taking care of this world.

52
00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:30.380
Now remove all of that.

53
00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:33.380
And God is not doing any of that.

54
00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:38.380
Can you imagine what it might be like to not be able to take a breath,

55
00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:45.380
to not have the sun shining, to not have this earth sustained by Him?

56
00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.380
Uninhabitable.

57
00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:51.380
It's kind of the way I try to paint a picture for hell for students

58
00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:57.380
to give them that sense of like, oh, God is doing all of this for me

59
00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:01.380
whether I choose Him or not, right?

60
00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.690
So then the question comes, well, wait a minute,

61
00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:07.380
how come God sends good people to hell?

62
00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.380
How come God sends anybody to hell?

63
00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:15.380
Well, the short answer is God doesn't send anybody, we send ourselves

64
00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:18.380
because we choose to not want Him.

65
00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:22.380
You know, I've often said even that God honors our choices

66
00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:26.380
and allows us to choose not Him and then gives us that very choice.

67
00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:31.380
So this week, small groups as always, but this week especially is super important

68
00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.740
because all that we're talking about is sort of going to come to a bit of a

69
00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:36.380
culmination

70
00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.380
in the sense that how can a God that we've already said is good that's allowing evil

71
00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.523
and all those kinds of things,

72
00:04:42.523 --> 00:04:47.380
how can He then have the existence of hell be alongside that, right?

73
00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:51.380
If God is so good and so loving and He allows this kind of evil,

74
00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.380
and this is the question that's been posed to me several times,

75
00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:59.380
is if God allows evil and allows the suffering to happen

76
00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:05.380
and He's so good, then why would He have hell as a punishment for not believing?

77
00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:08.380
Almost seems like there's a contradiction, right?

78
00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:12.239
So these are some of the questions that your students may bring up or some version

79
00:05:12.239 --> 00:05:12.380
of.

80
00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:15.380
Again, open discussion.

81
00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:22.380
If a student is not sure about hell, invite the discussion, invite the dialogue.

82
00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:27.380
Don't shoot them down and just point to scripture and kind of thump on the Bible

83
00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:28.380
like, well, this is what the Bible says.

84
00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:31.380
Well, yeah, and we've talked about the reliability of the text

85
00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.380
and the authority of what's in there.

86
00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:35.460
But hell is a very,

87
00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:39.380
very real reality that can be difficult for some people to deal with.

88
00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:43.196
So be patient with your students as you bring them along if they're not quite there

89
00:05:43.196 --> 00:05:43.380
yet.

90
00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.380
Allow them the time to process it.

91
00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:49.051
And then small groups are going to be one of those times where that's going to

92
00:05:49.051 --> 00:05:49.380
happen.

93
00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:55.380
And again, it's understanding that God wants us to choose Him.

94
00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.380
God wants us to be with Him.

95
00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.380
God invites us into relationship.

96
00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.380
He does not force us.

97
00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.380
And that is love in action.

98
00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.380
I want you to be with me.

99
00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:12.380
Imagine being married to somebody that you love that doesn't love you back.

100
00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:14.380
That doesn't seem to make any sense.

101
00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:14.717
Well,

102
00:06:14.717 --> 00:06:20.043
you made it through this week and you've almost made it through the rest of the

103
00:06:20.043 --> 00:06:20.380
year.

104
00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:25.380
We continue to pray for you here and we continue to pray for your students.

105
00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:33.776
And I hope that through this process of looking at hell and evil and suffering in a

106
00:06:33.776 --> 00:06:34.222
very,

107
00:06:34.222 --> 00:06:35.380
very real way

108
00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:39.380
has helped your students understand not only the point of suffering

109
00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:41.380
but the character of God a little bit better

110
00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:45.358
and that not only that this points to the existence of God in some sort of

111
00:06:45.358 --> 00:06:46.380
philosophical sense

112
00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:50.380
but that even in the midst of suffering God is right there with us

113
00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:53.380
feeling the pain along with us.

114
00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:58.380
I hope your students have a better picture of who God is and who Christ is

115
00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:00.380
and what their salvation means and all of that.

116
00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:03.380
You have four more lessons to go.

117
00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:09.101
Now would be a good time to take another inventory of your students and where they

118
00:07:09.101 --> 00:07:09.380
are.

119
00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:14.380
Go back to some of your original notes about how your students started off this year

120
00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:17.380
and how they were around Unit 4.

121
00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:19.380
Where are they now?

122
00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:23.380
And you got some students that have made some decisions.

123
00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.380
I hope and pray that you have.

124
00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:28.380
Do you have some students that still have significant questions?

125
00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.380
If you need to take some time and revisit some of those questions

126
00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:35.380
either as a group or individually or in small groups, whatever you need to.

127
00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.380
Don't rush this process.

128
00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:40.380
You've got four lessons to go.

129
00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:44.380
All of which are going to focus on wrapping things up

130
00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:46.380
and tying up some loose ends

131
00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:50.380
and helping to send your students onward and forward into the world

132
00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:54.380
with greater conviction, with greater confidence and with greater courage.

